# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Local state / data — never commit (docs/security-hardening-backlog OPS-02)
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
# SQLite's sidecars carry live page data — as sensitive as the .db itself — and `*.db` does
# NOT match them: -shm/-wal/-journal are a different suffix, not an extension. All three were
# tracked at one point, so every run left a dirty tree, which permanently violated the "no
# soak/replay on a dirty tree" rule. -journal is the rollback-mode sidecar; it appears whenever
# journal_mode is not WAL, so ignoring only the WAL pair leaves a gap.
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
*.duckdb
*.parquet
/data/
/replays/

# Secrets live in Windows Credential Manager (keyring), NEVER in the repo (Invariant 4)
.env
*.env
secrets.*
# ...but app/core/secrets.py is the keyring WRAPPER MODULE, not a secret file. The rule above
# silently untracked it from WP0 until RW-01 (a clean checkout then failed to import
# core.secrets while `git status` looked clean). Keep this exception.
!**/secrets.py
*.key
*.pem

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
